  "id": "161c20cf-8dbc-5727-8edf-3d8279239e9b",
  "slug": "old-fashioned-swedish-glogg",
  "name": "Old-Fashioned Swedish Gl\u00f6gg",
  "recipe_type": "drink",
  "brief_description": "Gl\u00f6gg is a fragrant Swedish spiced wine punch spiked with whiskey and rum. You'll feel the heat when you serve this mulled wine for the holidays!",
  "cuisine": "Swedish Scandinavian",
  "instructions": [
    {
      "position": 1,
      "text": "Heat port wine in a large stockpot with a lid over medium heat until just below the simmering point. Add bourbon and rum; heat until just below simmering. Save the bottles and their caps for storing leftover gl\u00f6gg."
    },
    {
      "position": 2,
      "text": "Meanwhile, place cinnamon stick, orange peel, cloves, and cardamom pods in the center of the cheesecloth square. Gather edges of the cheesecloth and tie with kitchen twine to secure; set aside."
    },
    {
      "position": 3,
      "text": "When wine mixture is very hot but not boiling, carefully light it with a long-handled match. Wearing a heatproof cooking mitt, carefully pour sugar into the flames; let mixture burn for 1 minute. Place the lid on the stockpot to extinguish the flames and turn off the heat. Let mixture cool, covered, about 10 minutes."
    },
    {
      "position": 4,
      "text": "Add the cheesecloth spice bundle, raisins, and almonds to warm wine mixture; let it cool to room temperature, about 1 hour."
    },
    {
      "position": 5,
      "text": "Strain cooled gl\u00f6gg and reserve the raisins and almonds."
    },
    {
      "position": 6,
      "text": "To serve: Pour gl\u00f6gg into a saucepan and warm over medium-low heat until hot but not simmering, about 5 minutes. Ladle 3 ounces of warmed gl\u00f6gg into a small coffee cup or a small Swedish-style gl\u00f6gg mug, and garnish each serving with a few reserved raisins and almonds."
    }
  ],
  "servings": 60,
  "cooking_time_minutes": 20,
  "preparation_time_minutes": 15,
